<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Range-Family–Aware Surrogates and Data-Dependent Guarantees</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix provides the full details for the theoretical results summarized in Section <a href="#S4.SS1.SSS3" title='4.1.3 Range-Family–Aware Surrogates and Data-Dependent Guarantees ‣ 4.1 Differentiable Estimator 𝐻_"diff" ‣ 4 Method ‣ Differentiable Entropy Regularization for Geometry and Neural Networks' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>A range-aware soft partition and entropy</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a range family on <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> of finite VC dimension <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{VC}}(\mathcal{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>VC</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{VC}}(\mathcal{R})</annotation></semantics></math>; in our geometric applications <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is the family of halfspaces.
Fix <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and parameters <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta=\{(w_{t},b_{t})\}_{t=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta=\{(w_{t},b_{t})\}_{t=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{t}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{t}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> define the <em id="A6.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">soft halfspace indicator</em></p>
<table id="A6.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}(x)\;=\;\sigma\!\left(\frac{w_{t}^{\top}x-b_{t}}{\tau}\right),\qquad\sigma(u)=\frac{1}{1+e^{-u}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.437em;" width="0.437em"><mi>σ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}(x)\;=\;\sigma\!\left(\frac{w_{t}^{\top}x-b_{t}}{\tau}\right),\qquad\sigma(u)=\frac{1}{1+e^{-u}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Each <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{1}{4\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{1}{4\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz relaxation of the hard indicator <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{1}\{w_{t}^{\top}x\geq b_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}\{w_{t}^{\top}x\geq b_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. A collection <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{h_{t}\}_{t=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{h_{t}\}_{t=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> induces <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\!\leq\!\sum_{i=0}^{d}\binom{m}{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.0539em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.0539em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\!\leq\!\sum_{i=0}^{d}\binom{m}{i}</annotation></semantics></math> soft <em id="A6.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">cells</em> via a differentiable gating scheme; one convenient choice is the normalized product:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{j}(x)\;=\;\frac{\prod_{t=1}^{m}\big(h_{t}(x)\big)^{\alpha_{jt}}\big(1-h_{t}(x)\big)^{\beta_{jt}}}{\sum_{\ell=1}^{K}\prod_{t=1}^{m}\big(h_{t}(x)\big)^{\alpha_{\ell t}}\big(1-h_{t}(x)\big)^{\beta_{\ell t}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{j}(x)\;=\;\frac{\prod_{t=1}^{m}\big(h_{t}(x)\big)^{\alpha_{jt}}\big(1-h_{t}(x)\big)^{\beta_{jt}}}{\sum_{\ell=1}^{K}\prod_{t=1}^{m}\big(h_{t}(x)\big)^{\alpha_{\ell t}}\big(1-h_{t}(x)\big)^{\beta_{\ell t}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{jt},\beta_{jt})\in\{0,1\}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{jt},\beta_{jt})\in\{0,1\}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> encodes whether cell <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> lies on the positive/negative side of range <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. For a finite point set <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the empirical soft cell masses <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}(S)=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}g_{j}(x_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}(S)=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}g_{j}(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and the <em id="A6.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">range-aware soft entropy</em></p>
<table id="A6.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H_{\mathrm{soft}}(S;\Theta,\tau)\;=\;-\sum_{j=1}^{K}q_{j}(S)\,\log q_{j}(S)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>soft</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.058em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\mathrm{soft}}(S;\Theta,\tau)\;=\;-\sum_{j=1}^{K}q_{j}(S)\,\log q_{j}(S).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The <em id="A6.SS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">range-partition entropy</em> <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\mathcal{R}}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\mathcal{R}}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> is the minimum (hard) entropy over partitions induced by ranges in <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (as in the original instance-optimal analysis). Our goal is to prove <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\mathrm{soft}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>soft</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\mathrm{soft}}</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="A6.SS1.p1.4.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">provably approximates</em> <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\mathcal{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\mathcal{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> when the hard partition has a non-trivial <em id="A6.SS1.p1.4.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">margin</em>, and to do so with <em id="A6.SS1.p1.4.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">data-dependent</em> rates.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Halfspace-aware consistency under margin</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first handle the most relevant family for convex-hull and maxima: halfspaces. Let <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be all halfspaces. A hard partition <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{C_{j}\}_{j=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{C_{j}\}_{j=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> induced by <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> halfspaces can be represented by a binary matrix <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(\alpha_{jt},\beta_{jt})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(\alpha_{jt},\beta_{jt})\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We say this partition has <em id="A6.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="A6.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-margin on <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></em> if for every <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in S</annotation></semantics></math> and every defining hyperplane <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}^{\top}x=b_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}^{\top}x=b_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> the signed distance satisfies <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|w_{t}^{\top}x-b_{t}|\geq\gamma\|w_{t}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|w_{t}^{\top}x-b_{t}|\geq\gamma\|w_{t}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Halfspace-aware soft consistency)<span id="Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be finite and suppose a hard partition <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{C_{j}\}_{j=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{C_{j}\}_{j=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is induced by <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> halfspaces with <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-margin on <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for any <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and any temperature <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\leq\gamma/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\leq\gamma/4</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists parameters <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\!\leq\!m^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\!\leq\!m^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> such that, with probability at least <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> over sampling <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. from any distribution supported on the same points,</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big\|q(S)-p(S)\big\|_{1}\;\leq\;\varepsilon_{\mathrm{smooth}}(\gamma,\tau)\;+\;c\,\sqrt{\frac{d\log m^{\star}+\log(2K/\delta)}{n}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>smooth</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big\|q(S)-p(S)\big\|_{1}\;\leq\;\varepsilon_{\mathrm{smooth}}(\gamma,\tau)\;+\;c\,\sqrt{\frac{d\log m^{\star}+\log(2K/\delta)}{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}(S)=|C_{j}\cap S|/|S|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}(S)=|C_{j}\cap S|/|S|</annotation></semantics></math> are the hard cell masses on <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> are the soft masses, <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathrm{smooth}}(\gamma,\tau)\leq e^{-\gamma/(4\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>smooth</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathrm{smooth}}(\gamma,\tau)\leq e^{-\gamma/(4\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a universal constant. Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|H_{\mathcal{R}}(S)-H_{\mathrm{soft}}(S;\Theta,\tau)\big|\;\leq\;\Big\|q(S)-p(S)\Big\|_{1}\,\log\!\frac{K}{\|q(S)-p(S)\|_{1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>soft</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|H_{\mathcal{R}}(S)-H_{\mathrm{soft}}(S;\Theta,\tau)\big|\;\leq\;\Big\|q(S)-p(S)\Big\|_{1}\,\log\!\frac{K}{\|q(S)-p(S)\|_{1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(1) <em id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Approximation of hard indicators.</em> By <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-margin and <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\leq\gamma/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\leq\gamma/4</annotation></semantics></math>, for each defining hyperplane the logistic <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma(\cdot/\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\cdot/\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> differs from the hard indicator by at most <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="e^{-\gamma/(4\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-\gamma/(4\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. Products of such factors (numerator of <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>) inherit an additive error bounded by <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathrm{smooth}}(\gamma,\tau)\leq e^{-\gamma/(4\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>smooth</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathrm{smooth}}(\gamma,\tau)\leq e^{-\gamma/(4\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math>, and normalization preserves <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> deviation across cells. This yields the deterministic term. 
<br class="ltx_break">(2) <em id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Uniform convergence.</em> The class <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{x\mapsto g_{j}(x)\}_{j\leq K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x\mapsto g_{j}(x)\}_{j\leq K}</annotation></semantics></math> has pseudo-dimension <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(d\log m^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(d\log m^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> since it is a composition of <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> sigmoids of linear functionals with a bounded-degree polynomial and a rational normalization; standard Rademacher/VC arguments give the stated <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\!\big(\sqrt{(d\log m^{\star}+\log(K/\delta))/n}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\!\big(\sqrt{(d\log m^{\star}+\log(K/\delta))/n}\big)</annotation></semantics></math> rate for the empirical means <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> around their population counterparts, uniformly over <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">(3) <em id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Entropy continuity.</em> For distributions on a <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>-simplex, <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|H(p)-H(q)|\leq\|p-q\|_{1}\log\!\frac{K}{\|p-q\|_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|H(p)-H(q)|\leq\|p-q\|_{1}\log\!\frac{K}{\|p-q\|_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., via Pinsker-type arguments or a mean-value bound on the entropy gradient). Combining (1)–(3) proves the claim. ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Data-dependent, range-agnostic bounds (unknowns removed)</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The next result avoids unknown latent parameters (e.g., an unknown optimal <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, unknown true margin <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>) by replacing them with <em id="A6.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">empirical</em> quantities computed on <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\gamma}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\gamma}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <em id="A6.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">empirical margin</em> of the chosen soft partition (the minimum signed distance of points in <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> to the learned separating hyperplanes, normalized by <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|w_{t}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|w_{t}\|</annotation></semantics></math>). Let <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\sigma}(\tau)=\tfrac{1}{4\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\sigma}(\tau)=\tfrac{1}{4\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> be the Lipschitz constant of <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma(\cdot/\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\cdot/\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>, and define</p>
<table id="A6.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Rad}_{n}(\mathcal{G}_{m})\;\leq\;C\,L_{\sigma}(\tau)\,\sqrt{\frac{d\log m}{n}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Rad</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Rad}_{n}(\mathcal{G}_{m})\;\leq\;C\,L_{\sigma}(\tau)\,\sqrt{\frac{d\log m}{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">a standard Rademacher bound for compositions of <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> linear separators with a 1-Lipschitz normalization (constant <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> hides benign log factors).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Data-dependent bound with empirical quantities)<span id="Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m,\tau&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m,\tau&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and learned parameters <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\big|H_{\mathcal{R}}(S)-H_{\mathrm{soft}}(S;\Theta,\tau)\big|\;\leq\;\left(e^{-\hat{\gamma}(S)/(4\tau)}+2\,\operatorname{Rad}_{n}(\mathcal{G}_{m})+\sqrt{\tfrac{\log(2/\delta)}{2n}}\right)\log\!\frac{K}{e^{-\hat{\gamma}(S)/(4\tau)}+2\,\operatorname{Rad}_{n}(\mathcal{G}_{m})+\sqrt{\tfrac{\log(2/\delta)}{2n}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>soft</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.169em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>Rad</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Rad</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|H_{\mathcal{R}}(S)-H_{\mathrm{soft}}(S;\Theta,\tau)\big|\;\leq\;\left(e^{-\hat{\gamma}(S)/(4\tau)}+2\,\operatorname{Rad}_{n}(\mathcal{G}_{m})+\sqrt{\tfrac{\log(2/\delta)}{2n}}\right)\log\!\frac{K}{e^{-\hat{\gamma}(S)/(4\tau)}+2\,\operatorname{Rad}_{n}(\mathcal{G}_{m})+\sqrt{\tfrac{\log(2/\delta)}{2n}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Identical to Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Halfspace-aware soft consistency). ‣ F.2 Halfspace-aware consistency under margin ‣ Appendix F Range-Family–Aware Surrogates and Data-Dependent Guarantees ‣ Differentiable Entropy Regularization for Geometry and Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> but replacing the unknown true margin <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> by the <em id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">empirical</em> margin <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\gamma}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\gamma}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> of the learned separators, and using a standard empirical Rademacher bound (symmetrization + contraction). The final step again uses entropy continuity on the simplex. ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Interpretation.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The bound depends <em id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">only on quantities you can compute from <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></em>: the empirical margin <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\gamma}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\gamma}(S)</annotation></semantics></math>, the chosen temperature <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, the model size <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, sample size <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. It removes the need to know unknown latent partition parameters. As <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\gamma}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\gamma}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> increases or <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> decreases (until numerical stability limits), the first term decays exponentially; as <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> grows, the second and third terms shrink as <math id="A6.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\big(\sqrt{(d\log m)/n}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\big(\sqrt{(d\log m)/n}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.4 </span>Beyond halfspaces: other range families</h3>

<div id="A6.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The same construction extends to other <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> by replacing the linear score <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\top}x-b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\top}x-b</annotation></semantics></math> with a differentiable signed distance <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{r}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{r}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> to range boundary <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., axis-aligned rectangles, slabs, wedges). Define <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{r}(x)=\sigma(s_{r}(x)/\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{r}(x)=\sigma(s_{r}(x)/\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> and reuse the same gating. The proofs of Theorems <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Halfspace-aware soft consistency). ‣ F.2 Halfspace-aware consistency under margin ‣ Appendix F Range-Family–Aware Surrogates and Data-Dependent Guarantees ‣ Differentiable Entropy Regularization for Geometry and Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>–<a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Data-dependent bound with empirical quantities). ‣ F.3 Data-dependent, range-agnostic bounds (unknowns removed) ‣ Appendix F Range-Family–Aware Surrogates and Data-Dependent Guarantees ‣ Differentiable Entropy Regularization for Geometry and Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> go through verbatim with <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{VC}}(\mathcal{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>VC</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{VC}}(\mathcal{R})</annotation></semantics></math> replacing <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding identical rates and the same empirical-margin–based exponential term.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.5 </span>A practical halfspace-aware estimator</h3>

<div id="A6.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To instantiate our theory in algorithms used in the paper, we replace the ball-based surrogate with a halfspace-aware version:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\text{diff}}^{\mathrm{half}}(S)\;:=\;H_{\mathrm{soft}}(S;\Theta_{\mathrm{half}},\tau)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mtext>diff</mtext><mi>half</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>soft</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>half</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\text{diff}}^{\mathrm{half}}(S)\;:=\;H_{\mathrm{soft}}(S;\Theta_{\mathrm{half}},\tau),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{\mathrm{half}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>half</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{\mathrm{half}}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained by (i) selecting <math id="A6.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> directions via data-dependent hyperplanes (e.g., maximum-margin separators or principal directions), and (ii) optimizing <math id="A6.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> by minimizing a validation estimate of the bound in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Data-dependent bound with empirical quantities). ‣ F.3 Data-dependent, range-agnostic bounds (unknowns removed) ‣ Appendix F Range-Family–Aware Surrogates and Data-Dependent Guarantees ‣ Differentiable Entropy Regularization for Geometry and Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. This drops directly into our training objective by replacing <math id="A6.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\text{diff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mtext>diff</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\text{diff}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\text{diff}}^{\mathrm{half}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mtext>diff</mtext><mi>half</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\text{diff}}^{\mathrm{half}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 1</span></span><span id="Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Plug-and-play replacement in objectives)<span id="Thmcorollary1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Replacing the ball-based <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\text{diff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">diff</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\text{diff}}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\text{diff}}^{\mathrm{half}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">diff</mtext><mi>half</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\text{diff}}^{\mathrm{half}}</annotation></semantics></math> preserves the differentiability of the training objective and, under the same empirical margin assumptions, enjoys the guarantees of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Data-dependent bound with empirical quantities). ‣ F.3 Data-dependent, range-agnostic bounds (unknowns removed) ‣ Appendix F Range-Family–Aware Surrogates and Data-Dependent Guarantees ‣ Differentiable Entropy Regularization for Geometry and Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. In particular, minimizing <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\text{diff}}^{\mathrm{half}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">diff</mtext><mi>half</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\text{diff}}^{\mathrm{half}}</annotation></semantics></math> drives <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\mathcal{R}}(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\mathcal{R}}(S)</annotation></semantics></math> down up to an explicitly bounded, data-dependent slack.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
